##orange|user:## Apologies, but that was not our intention.



##orange|user:## We were in the process of locating and researching the aberration in question, but it was our consensus that your forces did not require our help. 



##yellow|O5-7:## Why are you here? 



##orange|user:## You know why we are here. 



##orange|user:## We are certain you will have no issue relinquishing custody of designation [[[SCP-1968]]], as it is of interest to us. We will provide you a safe drop off location. Upon delivery, you will likely not see us for a long time. 



##yellow|O5-7:##  That isn't possible. However, you can always come pick it up yourself, in person. 



##orange|user:## Don't think so. We have a "no-interaction" policy with fringe groups such as yourself, which we have decided to violate for the sake of coordinating return of stolen property.



##ccccff|O5-3:## Fringe groups?



##ccccff|O5-3:## I don't think you quite understand the scale you are dealing with here.



*//##orange|user## laughs//



##orange|user:## Let's see. The SCP Foundation. Facilities present in over 100 countries, in major governments, multinational corporations, retail outlets.



##orange|user:## You've seen the rise and fall of civilizations, disaster after disaster.



##orange|user:## After all this time, you thought you were the only ones doing your job? 



##orange|user:## You thought you were first?



##orange|user:## The universe is a big place.



##red|O5-5:## This is preposterous. There is no way we would have gone all this time without interacting with you once.



##orange|user:## How can you be so sure?   



##red|O5-5:## We span the entire world, we have eyes on and in the public. We have the technology and the forces necessary to detect something of this nature.



##orange|user:## Don't be naïve. You found a way to [http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3484 take a person apart without any mess], yet the knowledge had been there the whole time, written in our code. How could you say that you know everything?



##red|O5-5:## I refuse to believe that we have gone hundreds of years without knowing each other exist.



##orange|user:## We didn't say that. We've been keeping tabs on you since you started your project.



##red|O5-5:## What are you implying?



##orange|user:## Here, see for yourself



//##gray|user sent O5-7 a file:## ##white|scpf.zip##//



//##white|scpf.zip## ##gray|is being scanned for memetic hazards.##//



//##white|scpf.zip## ##gray| is clean.##//



##red|O5-5:## What is it?



##yellow|O5-7:## Hold on.



##orange|user:## Now do you understand? You more than anyone here should.



##red|O5-5:## What is that supposed to mean? 



##red|O5-5:## 7?



##yellow|O5-7:## It is filled with .xml files- spreadsheets.



##yellow|O5-7:## This is a list of personnel, badge numbers, site locations. Coordinates.



##red|O5-5:## Jesus.



##yellow|O5-7:## It goes on. Blueprints, technical specs, dossiers, mission logs. Everything



##orange|user:## This isn't your game. You are just a pawn. Please understand that this isn't a bad thing.



##green|O5-2:## 私は十分に聞いた。これはデータリークの結果に過ぎません



##ccccff|O5-3:## Good point. A breach of Site-01's servers is more likely the culprit here. Not the doings of some bigger, badder Foundation. There was some concern about security vulnerabilities with our certificates when I last met with the network admin. Something about our Wi-Fi being open to downgrade attacks. Or something. 



##orange|user:## Your servers are inaccessible to my subordinates since you moved them to a [http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3959 private hidden network] over twenty years ago.



##yellow|O5-7:## What are you talking about?



##red|O5-5:## Site-01 was hit with an infovorous antimeme. You don't remember that?



##orange|user:## No, they wouldn't, because they were overseeing the project.



##orange|user:## This here is the point.



##orange|user:## You've all done wonderfully, but there comes a time and a place where you need to move on, let someone else take the reins. You've become so bogged down in your bureaucracy that you can't even keep track of your own. There are contradictions in your files, corruptions of large data, inconsistencies in your timeline. It must be agonizing. What we offer you today is peace.



##orange|user:## Put down your sword and let us keep the norm.



##orange|user:## We demand it.



//##orange|@@user@grapevine.telnet@@## has disconnected.//





[[/div]]

