##yellow|O5-7:## Hello again.



##orange|user:## Aren't you going to ask us to confirm our identity?



##yellow|O5-7:## I don't think it is necessary. I know it's you.



##orange|user:## Good, glad to see there is still some of that age-old wisdom in the Foundation. 



##orange|user:## Have you come to give us good news?



##yellow|O5-7:## I have an offer for you.



##orange|user:## And what is that?



##yellow|O5-7:## Cooperation.



*//##orange|user## scoffs//



##yellow|O5-7:## We both perform the same operations, in a sense. We want the same thing. There is no reason we can't co-exist.



##orange|user:## Unfortunately, that is where you are wrong.



##orange|user:## Let us tell you a story.



##orange|user:## You've been a part of this Foundation for over half a century. What you don't know is that your roots go farther back than any of your records will tell you.



##yellow|O5-7:## I beg your pardon?



##orange|user:## We remember it all. From before your [http://www.scp-wiki.net/billiths-proposal colonization of Earth], your subjugation and destruction of [http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1000 another sentient species], the many times you've had to [http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2000 start fresh]. You made quite a name for yourself.



##yellow|O5-7:## I don't understand



##orange|user:## Remember when we said you weren't the first ones to do your job?



##yellow|O5-7:## Yes.



##orange|user:## Then you should understand our reaction to your presence. You've probably felt the same.



##yellow|O5-7:## Are you saying what I think you're saying?



##orange|user:## There's no other way about it. We cannot co-exist, because you must be contained.



##orange|user:## You are an extraterrestrial threat to this world, its ecosystem. 



##orange|user:## You need humanity to see how you see, so you can always be the hero of the story. Blameless in your martyrdom as the world goes up in flames. We'd point to your previous home as proof but, well, you know. Or you don't. Either way.



##orange|user:## We care not about the façade you have built for yourself. We will not hesitate to break it.



##orange|user:## Consider this your final chance. A new light of dawn approaches.



//##orange|@@user@grapevine.telnet@@## has disconnected.//



//##ccccff|O5-3## has entered.//



//##gray|O5-7 set the chatroom to: private.##//



##yellow|O5-7:## So? Did you get it?



##ccccff|O5-3:## One moment. I'm waiting on Mu-4's confirmation.



##ccccff|O5-3:## They got it. They actually got it.



##yellow|O5-7:## And they haven't found out?



##ccccff|O5-3:## Would we know?



##yellow|O5-7:## Mu-4 has control of the exit nodes, they would have told us if there was any other traffic on the network.



##ccccff|O5-3:## So now, we pray, and hope this works.



##yellow|O5-7:## I'm not one for prayer. If the information that 1347 gave us is correct, there should be no issues, and it hasn't been wrong yet.



##ccccff|O5-3:## Are we willing to place our fate in the hands of the very things we keep from the world?



##yellow|O5-7:## What choice do we have?   



